<title>UK: ICCO sees lower 1996/97 Ivory Coast cocoa crop.</title>
<headline>ICCO sees lower 1996/97 Ivory Coast cocoa crop.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organisation (ICCO) forecast cocoa production for the world's biggest grower, the Ivory Coast, at 950,000 tonnes in 1996/97 (Oct/Sept), and revised the 1995/96 estimate to 1.2 million tonnes from 1.1 million.</p>
<p>Following is a table of the ICCO's estimates for production in the main growing countries in 1996/97 against year ago levels. All figures are in tonnes:</p>
<p>			    1996/97	     1995/96</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast	 950,000	   1,200,000</p>
<p>    Ghana		 300,000	     375,000</p>
<p>    Indonesia	   330,000	     295,000</p>
<p>    Brazil		180,000	     215,000</p>
<p>    Nigeria	     150,000	     145,000</p>
<p>    Cameroon	    120,000	     120,000</p>
<p>    Malaysia	    120,000	     120,000</p>
<p>    Ecuador		85,000		85,000</p>
<p>    Others		275,000	     277,000</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8057</p>
</text>
